1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,645
Start with a PowerPoint theme you already trust.

2
00:00:03,645 --> 00:00:10,934
Bento-deck-studio reads its colors, type, slide size, layouts, and candidate image assets without changing the source.

3
00:00:10,934 --> 00:00:17,312
Review the extracted theme tokens before you build, and let them shape the story.

4
00:00:17,662 --> 00:00:21,646
Next, give Copilot a topic, outline, or Markdown script.

5
00:00:21,646 --> 00:00:26,959
The authoring flow turns it into native bento slides, not flattened images.

6
00:00:26,959 --> 00:00:34,928
Each slide gets one message, clear hierarchy, and an editable layout you can revise without losing the message.

7
00:00:35,278 --> 00:00:41,869
Before writing the file, the deck builder checks Bento's signed release manifest and verifies the shell hash.

8
00:00:41,869 --> 00:00:47,685
A supplied image can become the favicon, or the site can generate a theme-colored monogram.

9
00:00:47,685 --> 00:00:52,726
The checks run before the deck is written, so release integrity comes first.

10
00:00:53,076 --> 00:00:58,172
By default, the result is a simple launch page with the presentation one click away.

11
00:00:58,172 --> 00:01:01,909
Choose the full companion site for a menu and story sections.

12
00:01:01,909 --> 00:01:11,082
Slides is the first menu item and opens a read-only deck in a new tab, while the deck stays editable and the site remains easy to host.

13
00:01:11,432 --> 00:01:18,312
Before sharing, validate the structure, review every slide in a browser, and check links and the favicon.

14
00:01:18,312 --> 00:01:22,360
The public deck copy removes speaker notes and collaboration credentials.

15
00:01:22,360 --> 00:01:29,645
Your theme, your narrative, and a more considered way to present, ready to share after one final review.
